# Bridge to the Home Assistant broker. See docs/PFC200.md and BACKLOG.
#
# WHY THE BRIDGE EXISTS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT DO. It is a TRANSPORT change, not
# an independence gain: while a room's sensor still reaches heatctl through
# Home Assistant, that room still depends on HA being up. Independence arrives
# per room, as each Shelly starts publishing here directly. What the bridge
# buys is that the two migrations - compute onto the PFC, sensors onto this
# broker - can happen in either order and one room at a time.
#
# Hosted on the PFC rather than on HA deliberately: this side's configuration
# is version-controlled in the heatctl repository, HA's broker configuration is
# the un-versioned thing docs/HA_INTEGRATION.md exists to compensate for.

connection ha
address 192.168.178.230:1883
remote_clientid pfc200-bridge
cleansession false
notifications true
notification_topic bridge/ha/state
try_private true
start_type automatic
restart_timeout 10 30

# --- OUT: what Home Assistant needs from us --------------------------------
# Telemetry and discovery, so the dashboards keep working once heatctl runs
# here. `sensors/#` too (owner): HA keeps seeing every room sensor even after
# the devices stop being HA's, which is what makes a per-room cutover
# reversible.
topic # out 2 heatctl/ heatctl/
topic # out 2 homeassistant/ homeassistant/
topic # out 2 sensors/ sensors/

# --- IN: what only Home Assistant can give us ------------------------------
# PERMANENT, and NARROWED to the two topics heatctl actually reads. Bridging
# rtl_433/# wholesale imported 625 retained topics, most of them fossils from
# 2022 - including a 13.4 degC outdoor temperature on the very topic that feeds
# the slab target, against a true 17.2. The add-on publishes these WITHOUT
# retain, so the fossil is what every new subscriber sees first and what it
# would keep forever if the station went silent.
# The WH65B stays on the HA-side rtl_433 path deliberately, as the
# outdoor-temperature contingency - see the resilience notes in BACKLOG.
topic 74930c0d-rtl433/devices/Fineoffset-WH65B/210/temperature_C in 2 rtl_433/ rtl_433/
topic 74930c0d-rtl433/devices/Fineoffset-WH32/245/temperature_C in 2 rtl_433/ rtl_433/

# Operator commands from the dashboard.
topic set/# in 2 heatctl/ heatctl/
topic hp/set/# in 2 heatctl/ heatctl/

# TRANSITIONAL, both of them. `roomtemp/#` disappears room by room as each
# Shelly moves to publishing here; `env/dew_point` disappears when D-045's
# local computation has agreed with the HA helper for long enough to retire it.
# Delete these two lines when that is done - leaving them would keep a
# dependency alive that nothing needs.
topic roomtemp/# in 2
topic env/dew_point in 2 heatctl/ heatctl/
remote_username plcbridge
remote_password <SET ON THE DEVICE - see docs/PFC200.local.md>
